### Architectural Audit & Root-Cause Remediation

#### 1. Mathematical Failure Mode: The Commensurability Deficit
The vulnerability manifests when aggregate physical reserves fall below the lower boundary polytope of combined Tier 1 (Metabolic Survival Baseline) and Tier 2-A (Systemic Infrastructural Upkeep). Under existing canonical provisions, the allocation engine requires a non-singular abiotic metric tensor $W$ derived from thermodynamic decay half-lives. However, because distinct elemental precursors (e.g., phosphorus, potable water, lithium, rare-earth catalysts) occupy orthogonal physical dimensions with independent physiological and infrastructural decay curves, the metric tensor cannot compute relative shadow prices under simultaneous structural deficits without an explicit, non-market conversion operator. Absent a lexicographic ordering axiom, the allocation algorithm produces undefined gradient divergences (division by zero / indeterminate state in shadow cost resolution), halting automated resource routing.

#### 2. Institutional Failure Mode: The Supermajority Deadlock
Art. 4.5.1 and Art. 3.6.2 previously mandated a 75% legislative supermajority to re-parameterize allocation weights or re-balance critical buffer reserves during emergency drawdowns. When available precursors fall below combined Tier 1/2-A thresholds, a 26% factional minority can block reserve re-parameterization to protect localized Tier 2 buffers, thereby freezing the allocation engine. This legislative paralysis cascades into uncoordinated, pro-rata brownouts, directly violating the unconditional baseline guarantee of Art. 1.3.1.

#### 3. Algorithmic and Constitutional Remedy
The patch implements a dual-layer deterministic safeguard:
*   **The Thermodynamic Lexicographic Priority Operator ($\mathcal{L}_{\min}$):** Formulates an explicit, invariant dimensional priority vector. Metabolic survival (caloric intake, hydration, active air purification, baseline thermal homeostasis) strictly dominates infrastructural replacement cycles. In the event of non-homothetic polytope contraction, the metric tensor collapses non-metabolic dimensions sequentially according to infrastructural resilience half-lives before any Tier 1 component is compressed.
*   **The Automated Fallback Ratchet & Sortition Escalation:** If the legislative assembly fails to resolve an emergency reserve re-parameterization within two diurnal cycles (48 hours) of a physical precursor deficit alert, the 75% voting threshold automatically ratchets downward by 5% per diurnal cycle to a floor of a simple absolute majority (50% + 1). If deadlock persists past 96 hours, authority transfers immediately to an emergency sortition panel drawn at random from directly affected frontline biome operators, operating under bounded lexicographic mandates that forbid baseline contraction.

